Monolithic vs Microservices vs Distributed

Monolithic = In monolithic architecture the whole app in one codebase deployed 
as one unit

Microservices = In microservices arch the app is split into small independent
services , each deployed on its own.

Distributed = In distributed system runs on multiple machines and communicate over 
a network.
Types : Coupled architecture and Decoupled architecture

Differences in Architecture

Monolithic vs Microservices = how you split the code (arc style )
Distributed = How many machines it runs on (nature of the deployment)

When to use what
Small teams or new project -> Monolithic
Code has grown teams are increasing -> Modular monolithic (micro)
Large project enterprise level = Distributed
